---
exclude_paths:
  - .github/

# The production profile demands things this repo deliberately does not do
# (fully qualified collection names are used, but every task also has to be
# idempotent by ansible-lint's static reading, which it cannot see through a
# shipped script). `safety` is the level whose findings have all been real here.
profile: safety

skip_list:
  # role-name requires ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$, which rules out github-ssh, first-login
  # and t3-service. That rule exists so a role can be addressed by a fully
  # qualified collection name, where the name has to be a valid Python
  # identifier. These roles live in roles/ in a playbook repository, are never
  # published to Galaxy and are never addressed that way — and the names are the
  # user-facing interface, because each is also its tag: `--only github-ssh` is
  # what the bash implementation took and what the docs say. Renaming them to
  # satisfy a packaging rule that does not apply would break that for nothing.
  - role-name

# Note what is *not* skipped. no-changed-when in particular: every command and
# shell task in these roles sets changed_when explicitly, several to `false`
# because running a vendor's own updater is not a change this playbook converges
# on. The two genuinely unavoidable exceptions carry an inline `# noqa` with the
# reason next to it, so they stay visible in review rather than disappearing
# into this file.
warn_list:
  - experimental
